Falsifies `paging::verification::the_chosen_leaf_is_the_largest_that_fits`.

The defect: `PageSize::largest_fitting` never answers 1 GiB (an off-by-one on the
level count, `>= 3` where it means `>= 2`). Nothing breaks: every leaf is still
aligned and inside its span, so the soundness harness beside this one stays green and
so does every translation. What is lost is the saving, silently, which is exactly the
failure a completeness property exists to catch: a direct map in 2 MiB leaves where
the machine offered 1 GiB ones.

Expected to fail: `assert!(literal_bytes(size) >= want, ...)` with `candidate` and
`largest` both `Size1GiB` and a 1 GiB-aligned span of at least 1 GiB.

